        var innerDict = new Dictionary<string, JsonElement>();
        foreach (var innerProp in outerProp.Value.EnumerateObject())
        {
            innerDict.Add(innerProp.Name, innerProp.Value.Clone());
        }
        allProfile.Add(outerProp.Name, innerDict);
    }
}
```

Wait - `span` is a `ReadOnlySpan<byte>`. `BinaryData.FromBytes` takes `ReadOnlyMemory<byte>`. Let me re-read the code.

Actually, looking at the code:
```csharp
var span = BinaryData.FromStream(stream).ToMemory().Span;
var allProfile = JsonSerializer.Deserialize<Dictionary<string, Dictionary<string, JsonElement>>>(span);
```

We can use JsonDocument directly. Since `span` is a `ReadOnlySpan<byte>`, we can use `JsonDocument.Parse(ReadOnlyMemory<byte>)`. But we have the memory from the line above. Change both lines to:

